00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:41.500
It's in the extended producer's cut, but I want to read to you a little bit of it from the shooting draft.

371
00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:42.000
Okay.

372
00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:43.800
It was actually really sweet.

373
00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:46.260
Jim says,

374
00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:50.060
Lately, there have been serious rumors that our company might go bankrupt.

375
00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.560
David Wallace asked me to keep morale high.

376
00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:54.120
Then there's B-roll.

377
00:18:54.640 --> 00:19:02.360
And the B-roll captures people taking turns going into Jim's office while Jim actually listens and jots down notes.

378
00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.220
Angela goes in, Kevin, Kelly, Stanley.

379
00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:07.440
Jim's talking head continues.

380
00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:10.760
I asked around what people wanted with Christmas.

381
00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:12.740
Get creative, I said.

382
00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:14.960
And people weren't really creative exactly.

383
00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:20.240
They said Secret Santa, karaoke, food, pretty much what we usually have, which is great.

384
00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:24.440
Then there's B-roll of Jim and Dwight dusting off old decorations.

385
00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.380
Jim continues to talk.

386
00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:30.700
People usually argue about food, so I told everyone to bring their favorites.

387
00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:32.320
Then there's B-roll.

388
00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.540
Angela laying out carrots and celery.

389
00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:37.260
Kevin with an enormous chocolate cake.

390
00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:39.120
Pam brings in a lasagna.

391
00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:43.880
And finally, Creed emptying a large can of beans into a glass serving bowl.

392
00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:45.200
Jim continues.

393
00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:49.760
I made a very organized sign-up sheet for karaoke so there's no fighting.

394
00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:54.780
B-roll of Jim holding up a clipboard next to the karaoke machine with a

395
00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:57.480
must-take-turns written on it in red letters.

396
00:19:58.060 --> 00:20:00.700
Kelly, Andy, and Kevin crowd around to sign up.

397
00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:02.640
Jim continues talking.

398
00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:05.400
And no crying.

399
00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:07.900
Jim hangs up a banner in the conference room.

400
00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:09.140
It says, Merry Christmas.

401
00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:10.680
Santa hates tears.

402
00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:14.740
And then lastly, Jim says,

403
00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:17.860
I made Phyllis Santa, fulfilling a lifelong dream.

404
00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:20.240
Phyllis hugs Jim and will not let go.

405
00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.060
Jim tries to subtly break free.

406
00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:25.120
And then Jim ends this talking head with this.

407
00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:27.460
I'm doing a good job, I think.

408
00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.340
Because this year, I care.

409
00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.300
I know.

410
00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:30.940
It's weird.

411
00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:32.980
He shrugs, happy.

412
00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.440
That is so sweet.

413
00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:36.320
I know.

414
00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:37.800
It was a great talking head.

415
00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:41.860
And it really showed how Jim was invested in making this a good party.

416
00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:43.600
This is good management.

417
00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:46.420
This just reminds me of how Greg Daniels would treat us.

418
00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.200
He would come around and he would say,

419
00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:51.080
What do you think should happen to your character this year?

420
00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:51.880
Yes.

421
00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.040
And you'd be like, I have ideas.

422
00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.760
Thank you for asking.

423
00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:59.660
So now Erin is going to make an announcement to the bullpen.

424
00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:05.520
She is pleading with whoever is her secret Santa to please stop sending gifts.

425
00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:11.620
Her secret Santa is doing a 12 Days of Christmas themed gift for her.

426
00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:15.980
And she says that her cat killed the turtle dove.

427
00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:19.040
The French hens are making a nest in her hair.

428
00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:22.620
She has scratches down her face.

429
00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:24.840
She's having a hard time with this gift.

430
00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.140
Oh, my gosh.

431
00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:27.860
She seems really miserable.

432
00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:35.460
Well, I wanted to share with you guys that the DVD commentary for this episode is Ellie Kemper, Mindy Kaling, and Claire Scanlon.

433
00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:36.640
Oh, great.

434
00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:37.000
Yeah.

435
00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:40.240
And they talked a little bit about this scratch on Ellie's face.

436
00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:46.880
Mindy shared that they had a test model that they did a few different types of scratches on and took pictures of.

437
00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:50.360
And then Mindy had to pick which scratch she liked.

438
00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:50.920
Yes.

439
00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:55.440
Randy said our makeup artist, Laverne, created the effects of the scratch.

440
00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:59.880
And I guess Randall and Paul both were really pleased with the first try.

441
00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:00.980
And that's the one they picked.

442
00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:05.260
And he said Laverne's team was masterful at executing this gag.

443
00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:10.460
Well, we had a fan catch during this scene at reception from Ursula N.

444
00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.360
in Toledo, Ohio, who says,

445
00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:16.520
At 2 minutes and 33 seconds, there is a card on Aaron's desk.

446
00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:22.980
Is that card the one where Michael photoshopped himself into Carol's family ski trip back in Season 3?

447
00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:24.740
Because it looks just like it.

448
00:22:25.700 --> 00:22:26.960
I zoomed in on it.

449
00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:28.420
It absolutely looks like it.

450
00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:29.560
I think it is.

451
00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:32.440
I think Michael is still setting that card out.

452
00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:34.620
That is brilliant and perfect.

