00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:21.120
I asked Randy Cordray, how did we pull off these shots with the geese and the swans?

465
00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:25.720
He said, once again, we used Bob Dunn's animal rentals in Silmar, California.

466
00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:32.220
We needed seven swans in the lobby, and they required three days of prep and rehearsal.

467
00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:36.320
He said swans can be very aggressive toward people that they don't know.

468
00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:37.180
Oh, yeah.

469
00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:43.620
So, the extra days of prep were to just let them walk around this lobby area and meet Ed HelMs.

470
00:23:43.880 --> 00:23:48.440
And, lady, I remember one day at lunch, Ed was eating, like, really faSt.

471
00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:53.960
And he said he had to finish eating quickly because he had to go spend time with the swans.

472
00:23:54.600 --> 00:23:55.380
Oh, my gosh.

473
00:23:55.380 --> 00:23:56.120
I don't doubt it.

474
00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:57.400
They had to get to know him.

475
00:23:57.640 --> 00:24:00.360
I was once chased by a very aggressive duck.

476
00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:04.140
In Indonesia, they would use, like, ducks and stuff to protect, like.

477
00:24:04.520 --> 00:24:05.580
Like a guard duck?

478
00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:07.080
Yeah, like a guard duck.

479
00:24:07.260 --> 00:24:08.460
And I was on a walk.

480
00:24:08.460 --> 00:24:09.240
It was up in the mountains.

481
00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:10.960
And I was, like, probably, like, 11.

482
00:24:11.100 --> 00:24:12.580
And this duck, like, chased me.

483
00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:13.320
I was terrified.

484
00:24:13.620 --> 00:24:14.580
I was like, oh, my God.

485
00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:15.980
They're scary.

486
00:24:16.240 --> 00:24:16.500
Yeah.

487
00:24:16.800 --> 00:24:18.040
I mean, they'll come for you.

488
00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:18.880
They'll come for you.

489
00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:25.460
Well, the six geese that were in Erin's car also had to do three days of prep.

