00:39:36.660 --> 00:39:40.200
And Beth said, I never noticed that speculum was on the liSt.

835
00:39:40.380 --> 00:39:44.420
But during a recent rewatch, I noticed and almost died laughing.

836
00:39:44.880 --> 00:39:49.060
So I found a list of all the things that Dwight thinks.

837
00:39:49.220 --> 00:39:50.700
This is what's on his piece of paper.

838
00:39:50.900 --> 00:39:51.260
Okay.

839
00:39:51.520 --> 00:39:53.820
In answer to your question, Beth, this would be the writers.

840
00:39:54.100 --> 00:39:55.640
The writers would have come up with this liSt.

841
00:39:55.640 --> 00:39:59.900
Phil Shea would have gone to the writers and said, what do you want me to write on this

842
00:39:59.900 --> 00:40:01.140
piece of paper for Dwight?

843
00:40:01.340 --> 00:40:05.800
And he would have had to write this list over and over and over and over again on various

844
00:40:05.800 --> 00:40:09.740
pads of paper because every take, Rain was going to scratch one out.

845
00:40:09.900 --> 00:40:13.440
So here was the list of things that Dwight thought this might be.

846
00:40:13.800 --> 00:40:22.940
An aardvark trap, beaver trap, gun, chipmunk trap, possum trap, skunk trap, lobster trap,

847
00:40:22.940 --> 00:40:28.140
man trap, lathe, abdominizer, speculum.

848
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:33.820
He was mostly convinced it was some sort of trap, an animal trap.

849
00:40:35.780 --> 00:40:39.720
Santa Phyllis is now going to do the tree lighting reveal.

850
00:40:39.980 --> 00:40:41.960
And it's so festive and cheery.

851
00:40:42.080 --> 00:40:43.380
I love Phyllis in this scene.

852
00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:44.000
I know.

853
00:40:44.160 --> 00:40:45.280
I absolutely love it.

854
00:40:45.600 --> 00:40:47.840
Michael is starting to get real sour.

855
00:40:48.360 --> 00:40:49.080
Oh, yeah.

856
00:40:49.560 --> 00:40:52.100
So he has this talking head.

857
00:40:52.940 --> 00:40:57.920
Where he says, I don't need a lot for Christmas, like diamonds or brooch, pendants.

858
00:40:58.400 --> 00:41:00.400
He just wants to be Santa.

859
00:41:00.900 --> 00:41:06.380
And this whole time, he is, like, reversing his Santa costume.

860
00:41:06.620 --> 00:41:11.580
Taking this decorative Christmas robe off his credenza, making it into a belt.

861
00:41:11.800 --> 00:41:14.780
I want to give a shout out to Steve's skills right here.

862
00:41:14.920 --> 00:41:16.480
I put it in my document.

863
00:41:16.480 --> 00:41:20.040
I need everyone to appreciate how hard this is to do.

864
00:41:20.040 --> 00:41:21.440
Yes, I wrote it, too.

865
00:41:21.560 --> 00:41:23.240
I put two little stars by it.

866
00:41:23.320 --> 00:41:25.480
I said, go to 9 minutes, 52 seconds.

867
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:27.920
Michael goes from Santa to Jesus.

868
00:41:28.140 --> 00:41:34.100
And Steve had to do all the dialogue, change his outfit, put the belt on in one shot.

869
00:41:34.220 --> 00:41:35.320
There are no cutaways.

870
00:41:36.140 --> 00:41:37.440
This is truly amazing.

871
00:41:37.440 --> 00:41:43.800
I cannot express to you how hard it is to do even ordinary business while you're acting.

872
00:41:44.080 --> 00:41:50.040
How many times would I have to do a scene where I'm supposed to walk in with a bag of groceries,

873
00:41:50.340 --> 00:41:52.720
