Then they needed another Santa.

1072
00:50:47.480 --> 00:50:48.300
Then they needed Jesus.

1073
00:50:48.640 --> 00:50:49.880
And now they need Michael.

1074
00:50:50.220 --> 00:50:52.560
And that's one suit Phyllis can't fit into.

1075
00:50:52.560 --> 00:50:55.520
At 14 minutes, 38 seconds.

1076
00:50:55.760 --> 00:50:57.380
I'd like to point out a snow alert.

1077
00:50:57.780 --> 00:50:59.000
There is now.

1078
00:50:59.220 --> 00:51:00.660
Do we have a snow alert?

1079
00:51:00.860 --> 00:51:01.580
We have a snow alert.

1080
00:51:02.600 --> 00:51:08.100
There is some snow falling gently behind Michael out his window.

1081
00:51:08.500 --> 00:51:12.680
It's evening now and it's begun snowing.

1082
00:51:13.240 --> 00:51:14.720
This will be important later.

1083
00:51:14.720 --> 00:51:18.780
Well, the way you solve any crisis is you buy pizza.

1084
00:51:19.260 --> 00:51:19.880
Lots of it.

1085
00:51:20.360 --> 00:51:23.320
Michael's going to send Dwight with his password.

1086
00:51:23.620 --> 00:51:26.660
You know, you have fun at the...

1087
00:51:26.660 --> 00:51:28.100
Uh, uh, uh, uh.

1088
00:51:28.800 --> 00:51:29.480
Yeah.

1089
00:51:29.760 --> 00:51:33.620
So his PIN is 9622.

1090
00:51:34.320 --> 00:51:35.900
That is YMCA.

1091
00:51:36.460 --> 00:51:42.460
The candy bag had some really fun alternates for what Michael's PIN number might be.

1092
00:51:42.460 --> 00:51:42.980
Oh, yeah?

1093
00:51:43.640 --> 00:51:44.760
Here's the first one.

1094
00:51:45.340 --> 00:51:49.520
I don't want to say it, but it's the year everyone was scared by Y2K.

1095
00:51:52.880 --> 00:51:53.720
Here's another one.

1096
00:51:54.240 --> 00:51:57.920
I don't want to say it, but it's the year we partied like it's 1999.

1097
00:51:59.780 --> 00:52:00.740
Here's another one.

1098
00:52:01.720 --> 00:52:05.700
I don't want to say it, but it's the first line in a famous song about the alphabet.

1099
00:52:07.380 --> 00:52:08.920
And then this was my favorite.

1100
00:52:09.580 --> 00:52:11.200
When Dwight says, what is your PIN?

1101
00:52:11.380 --> 00:52:20.040
Michael was going to say, 938-562-08771-6689-473.

1102
00:52:20.900 --> 00:52:24.360
I was just going to be like this ridiculously long number.

1103
00:52:24.560 --> 00:52:28.520
Those were all of our candy bag must shoot alternates for this.

1104
00:52:28.520 --> 00:52:34.100
And we stayed with the shooting draft scripted YMCA.

1105
00:52:35.120 --> 00:52:39.540
Aaron's going to ask Andy, what was he thinking, giving her all of those gifts?

1106
00:52:39.760 --> 00:52:40.500
But you know what?

1107
00:52:40.600 --> 00:52:41.500
Andy's not going to give up.

1108
00:52:41.580 --> 00:52:42.720
He's not going to throw in the towel.

1109
00:52:42.940 --> 00:52:43.780
Not going to happen.

1110
00:52:43.900 --> 00:52:44.740
No, he's not.

1111
00:52:44.900 --> 00:52:45.200
Mm-mm.

1112
00:52:45.660 --> 00:52:47.760
And later on, I'm glad he didn't.

1113
00:52:48.800 --> 00:52:50.180
Michael addresses the group.

1114
00:52:50.680 --> 00:52:51.900
He's got the pizza.

1115
00:52:52.560 --> 00:52:53.700
It's sitting there.

1116
00:52:53.700 --> 00:52:55.920
I think we'd all like to eat it.

1117
00:52:56.040 --> 00:52:58.540
But of course, Michael has to give a big speech firSt.

1118
00:52:59.120 --> 00:53:06.540
And then he does what only Michael can do, which is he tells everybody the news that he

1119
00:53:06.540 --> 00:53:10.680
was supposed to keep to himself, which is that we're going out of business.

1120
00:53:11.120 --> 00:53:14.500
Well, everyone has a pretty strong reaction to this news.

1121
00:53:15.140 --> 00:53:17.320
Dwight goes out and kicks the Christmas tree down.

1122
00:53:17.580 --> 00:53:17.720
Yeah.

1123
00:53:18.720 --> 00:53:22.720
Ellie and Mindy shared on the commentary that the day we shot this scene,

1124
00:53:22.720 --> 00:53:24.540
when Dwight's kicking the tree down.

1125
00:53:25.140 --> 00:53:31.400
The episode Niagara was airing that evening, and everyone wanted to wrap so we could get

1126
00:53:31.400 --> 00:53:32.980
to Greg's to watch Niagara.

1127
00:53:33.340 --> 00:53:38.020
I guess Greg had invited the whole cast over for a viewing party.

1128
00:53:38.240 --> 00:53:42.240
So I dug in my digital clutter, and I found the email invite.

1129
00:53:42.540 --> 00:53:43.300
Oh, my gosh.

1130
00:53:43.300 --> 00:53:45.580
I totally remember this viewing party, by the way.

1131
00:53:45.660 --> 00:53:45.920
Yeah.

1132
00:53:45.920 --> 00:53:47.060
He says,

1133
00:53:47.460 --> 00:53:53.020
Hey, guys, please come to my house for a viewing party for Niagara at 730, October 8th.

1134
00:53:53.180 --> 00:53:56.180
Dinner, and we will watch Jim and Pam get married.

1135
00:53:56.600 --> 00:53:57.400
Love, Greg.

1136
00:53:57.980 --> 00:54:03.920
Well, he and his wife, Suzanne, threw this party that was almost like a wedding reception.

1137
00:54:04.500 --> 00:54:08.640
They had little M&Ms printed with Jim and Pam.

1138
00:54:08.640 --> 00:54:11.360
And little napkins, like you would get at a wedding.

1139
00:54:11.680 --> 00:54:11.960
Yes.

1140
00:54:12.120 --> 00:54:13.660
It was so sweet.

1141
00:54:14.300 --> 00:54:16.060
They had amazing food.

1142
00:54:16.060 --> 00:54:17.640
It was really fun.

1143
00:54:17.920 --> 00:54:21.440
The tables had, you know, the little confetti you can sprinkle that had the little wedding

1144
00:54:21.440 --> 00:54:21.920
bells.

1145
00:54:21.960 --> 00:54:23.220
It was so cute.

1146
00:54:23.480 --> 00:54:25.300
I totally remember going to that.

1147
00:54:25.420 --> 00:54:26.020
I went with Lee.

1148
00:54:26.680 --> 00:54:30.860
So just know, while we were filming this conference room scene of Michael spilling the

1149
00:54:30.860 --> 00:54:34.760
beans and Dwight kicking the tree, we were like, all right, let's get these lines so

1150
00:54:34.760 --> 00:54:35.960
we can make it to Greg's.

1151
00:54:35.960 --> 00:54:38.140
Greg and Suzanne were always so generous.

1152
00:54:38.520 --> 00:54:43.680
They invited us into their home many, many times over these nine years of doing the office.

1153
00:54:43.940 --> 00:54:48.420
It was a really warm and personal touch, and it bonded us from the beginning.

1154
00:54:48.640 --> 00:54:49.600
It was really cool.

1155
00:54:49.780 --> 00:54:50.740
And they still are.

1156
00:54:50.860 --> 00:54:53.760
Greg invited us all over for Sunday brunch, and we all went.

1157
00:54:53.900 --> 00:54:54.900
We did, just recently.

1158
00:54:54.920 --> 00:54:55.540
Just recently.

1159
00:54:56.180 --> 00:55:00.540
Well, Michael tells everyone, listen, I'll get David on the phone so he can explain

1160
00:55:00.540 --> 00:55:01.080
things.

1161
00:55:01.340 --> 00:55:03.460
And Jim's like, I don't think so, Michael.

1162
00:55:03.460 --> 00:55:06.320
I've been trying to reach him all day, and he's not taking my calls.

1163
00:55:06.860 --> 00:55:10.180
And Michael is like, I know how to get a hold of him.

1164
00:55:10.460 --> 00:55:10.720
Mm-hmm.

1165
00:55:10.860 --> 00:55:11.920
He's proud of this.

1166
00:55:12.060 --> 00:55:12.640
It's amazing.

1167
00:55:13.020 --> 00:55:14.860
He knows where David's kids go to school.

1168
00:55:15.240 --> 00:55:18.800
So first he calls the school, pretends to be their pediatrician.

1169
00:55:19.580 --> 00:55:25.420
Then he gets patched through to David's secretary, and then he talks in his little girl voice.

1170
00:55:25.580 --> 00:55:27.140
And pretends to be David's daughter.

1171
00:55:27.140 --> 00:55:32.180
So, of course, when David answers the phone, he's like, what's up, sweetie?

1172
00:55:32.480 --> 00:55:32.900
Mm-hmm.

1173
00:55:33.100 --> 00:55:36.600
Because David thinks it's his daughter who's at the pediatrician's office.

1174
00:55:36.920 --> 00:55:38.360
Oh, my God, Michael.

1175
00:55:38.860 --> 00:55:40.300
I mean, it's kind of amazing.

1176
00:55:40.880 --> 00:55:48.080
In Michael's office, we have, for the first time, the whole entire Dunder Mifflin bullpen and warehouse.

1177
00:55:48.640 --> 00:55:49.140
Yes.

1178
00:55:49.520 --> 00:55:50.520
All of us.

1179
00:55:50.700 --> 00:55:52.600
Hovering over the speakerphone.

1180
00:55:53.260 --> 00:55:57.120
David reveals, Michael, first of all, you were never supposed to tell everybody.

1181
00:55:57.420 --> 00:55:59.900
But second of all, I wasn't talking about you.

1182
00:56:00.540 --> 00:56:02.420
All of your jobs are safe.

1183
00:56:02.420 --> 00:56:04.340
It's just this upper management.

1184
00:56:04.760 --> 00:56:07.240
You would have thought the office won the Super Bowl.

1185
00:56:07.320 --> 00:56:08.020
I know.

1186
00:56:08.380 --> 00:56:10.420
Everyone goes nuts.

1187
00:56:10.660 --> 00:56:14.580
Michael jumps off his desk and does this crowd surfing move.

1188
00:56:15.280 --> 00:56:18.040
Mindy shared on the commentary that that was Steve's idea,

1189
00:56:18.400 --> 00:56:21.800
